WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.961
The Five Points District in Denver,
Colorado, has

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:05.714
a legacy of African-American excellence.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.551
Long time business owners
like Franklin and Maedella Stiger

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:13.555
take pride in carrying that torch forward
as the neighborhood changes.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:15.724
The Frank and Miss Mae

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:18.643
Thank you so much
for allowing me to come in here today.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.770
When people talk about five points,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.065
they always say,
you have to come see the Stigers.

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:25.442
And they've been.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:27.485
Loving you guys
for the past 40 years, correct?

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.071
I've been here for 40 or better.

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:35.827
And I serve the people well.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.247
And so over the past 40 years,

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:43.334
how many people from the community
did you employ here at the Barbershop?

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:47.172
About three off and on,
you know, and during my time.

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:50.675
You had the natural and Jerry curl.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:51.134
Uh huh.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:55.221
And that's what brought

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.598
the money in.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:59.142
Miss Mae you had a jerry curl? Yes.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.270
Did you have a Jerry Curl?

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.521
And an Afro!

00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:06.733
That was my natural. Okay that was your natural.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:11.112
But then too for the community
with the projects being over in Arapaho,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.657
the little kids would come in
and said, Mr.

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.743
Stiger, Can I sweep the floor?

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.870
Can I do this? You know for lunch money.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.915
And he used to always have one
or two of them, you know,

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.708
come and help clean up the shop

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:25.460
and give them money.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.339
And they would take that money
and then work their school lunch money

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:30.673
for the week.

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:34.302
One of the kids
 turned out to be a doctor. Wow.

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.971
Whenever he come to Colorado,
he comes to the shop.

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:38.139
I love that.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:42.435
I just love that you guys are such
a staple in this community

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.645
and you're still here.

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.815
I'm always looking for ways
to support black businesses,

00:01:46.898 --> 00:01:50.693
but the Stigers remind me
that it's not just about buying black.

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:52.195
These small businesses

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:55.990
are the foundation of their communities,
creating the opportunities,

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:00.286
role models and healthy environments
that for so much of American history,

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.664
black people couldn't find elsewhere.

